# ── PROTECTIVE .gitignore ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# ~/Source is wired to the PUBLIC repo siddeepak2023.github.io.
# Everything below is excluded so an accidental `git add -A` can NEVER
# publish source code, secrets, data, or personal files to the public web.

# Secrets — never publish
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*serviceAccount*.json
**/*credentials*.json
**/firebase-adminsdk*.json
*.pem
*.key

# Product source code (has its own repos / secrets)
BizFalconAI/
clipforge/
clipfalcon/
Universe-Data-Visualization/
HypeClip AI/

# Data-analysis projects (raw data / not for public site)
Netflix-Stock-Sales-Prediction/
spotify_ab_test/
tmobile_churn/
Pirani/

# Cut projects — unpublished 2026-07-27. These were reachable by URL on the live
# site with nothing linking to them, still carrying claims the portfolio dropped.
# Files stay on disk; they must not go back to the public web.
#   Spotify A/B  — synthetic data behind a "$83.9M projected annual revenue" figure
#   NFL betting  — payload pulled earlier, the dashboard was left behind
#   DermIQ       — dropped for good; generated/synthetic clinic data
/spotify_ab_dashboard.html
/sports_betting_dashboard.html
dermiq/

# Olist + Retail: CODE is public (see each dir's README), DATA is not. Both source
# datasets are third-party downloads with their own redistribution terms, and the
# Olist master table alone is 36 MB. Each project's README documents how to fetch
# the raw data and regenerate every intermediate.
Olist_ecommerce_analysis/*.csv
Olist_ecommerce_analysis/*.xlsx
Olist_ecommerce_analysis/*.db
retail-customer-intelligence/*.csv
retail-customer-intelligence/*.xlsx
retail-customer-intelligence/*.db
retail-customer-intelligence/dashboard_data.json
retail-customer-intelligence/model_metrics.json
retail-customer-intelligence/association_rules.json
retail-customer-intelligence/segment_recommendations.json

# Coursework / archives / personal
CS1436/
Java/
LetterOrDigit/
Deepak.Sid/
Private Problems Archive/

# Friday — personal AI OS. LOCAL-ONLY. Never publish (faith/health/people/journal).
friday/

# cofounder — internal business operating layer. LOCAL-ONLY. Never publish
# (decision ledger rationale, pricing decisions, competitor analysis, audit findings).
cofounder/

# Personal documents
*.pdf
*.docx
Siddharth_Deepak_Resume.*

# Internal notes / specs (not for the public site — specs now live in BizFalconAI/ product dirs)
LAUNCH-AND-DEPLOY.md

# Python environments + bytecode. The venv is hundreds of MB and is one
# `git add -A` away from the public site, so it is ignored explicitly rather
# than relied upon to stay untracked.
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Build / OS junk
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
dist/
.claude/

# Product docs + scratch — never publish
insightpilot/
portfolio/
.Rhistory

# Flight-delay project: pipeline generates synthetic data, so the "72M real BTS
# flights" framing is not supportable. Kept locally, excluded from the public site
# until it is rebuilt on real BTS data.
flight-delay-intelligence/
flight_delay_dashboard.html

# NBA project source lives in its own repo (github.com/siddeepak2023/nba-intelligence).
# nba_dashboard.html is NO LONGER ignored: the old hand-written one carried the
# bogus -110 backtest, but the current file is generated by 08_build_dashboard.py
# with every figure interpolated from the pipeline, so it cannot drift. Rebuild it
# rather than editing it by hand.
nba-intelligence/

# NBA betting payload: strategy_a/strategy_b price every game at a constant -110,
# so the +35.8% ROI and $34K P&L figures are computed against a market that does not
# exist. The dashboard and backtest script were pulled on 2026-07-26; this payload was
# missed and stayed publicly fetchable at /dashboard_data.json. Kept locally only.
# Anchored with a leading slash — dermiq/data/ and quant-edge/data/ have legitimate
# tracked files of the same name.
/dashboard_data.json

# The two data projects each keep a local copy of their dashboard. The PUBLISHED
# copies are the ones at repo root, and only those get corrections applied — so
# never publish the in-project duplicates or they will contradict the live pages.
Olist_ecommerce_analysis/olist_dashboard.html
retail-customer-intelligence/retail_dashboard.html

# Shell reference page for dusk-dash.css / dash-charts.js — dev aid, not a
# published page. Kept so the mark specs stay eyeball-checkable.
_shelltest.html

# Netflix forecast dashboard — unpublished 2026-07-28. Real data, but no baseline
# (a naive random walk beats Prophet on daily equities) and a live bug: the holdout is
# fixed at 90 days in app.py:152 while forecast length comes from a UI slider, so
# merge_asof(direction='nearest') scores uncovered test days against a stale constant
# and the displayed RMSE changes when the user moves a slider that cannot affect it.
netflix_dashboard.html


# T-Mobile churn dashboard: real project with its own repo, but orphaned — linked from
# nowhere on the portfolio while LinkedIn advertised its 79%/0.834/$334K figures. Those
# numbers have never been through the audit the other projects went through, so it is
# unpublished until they are verified. Same treatment as netflix_dashboard.html.
churn_dashboard.html

# The full 6.79 MB-per-million star layer (52 MB). Git keeps every blob forever and
# Pages will not serve LFS, so the upgrade tier is hosted outside this repo; the viewer
# skips it gracefully when the fetch fails.
cosmos/stars_o.bin

# ── Founder-private: decks, briefs, architecture. NEVER on the public site.
bizfalcon-private/

# Coursework and unrelated apps living in this tree. Untracked today, but this repo
# publishes from root — one `git add -A` would put them on the public web.
#   4381-Final-Prep — class notebooks, exams, cheat sheets (93 MB)
#   ChristApp       — separate Firebase app: firestore.rules, security tests (1.1 GB)
4381-Final-Prep/
ChristApp/
